      },
      "availability": [
        {
          "_id": ObjectId("date_id"), // Unique identifier for each availability record
          "start_date": ISODate("YYYY-MM-DD"), // Check-in date
          "end_date": ISODate("YYYY-MM-DD"), // Check-out date
          "is_available": boolean // Indicates whether the room is available or not
        }
      ],
      "rates": [
        {
          "_id": ObjectId("rate_plan_id"), // Unique identifier for each rate plan
          "plan_code": "Rate Plan Code",
          "base_price": NumberDecimal // Base price for the rate plan
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

This schema allows for managing multiple hotel properties, with each property having an array of rooms. Each room has its unique identifier, number, type, capacity, availability records (with check-in and check-out dates and availability status), and rate plans. This schema is designed to minimize disk usage by denormalizing some data and utilizing MongoDB's efficient indexing and querying capabilities.

The `ObjectId`, `ISODate`, and `NumberDecimal` types are built-in data types provided by MongoDB. The `avg.arraySize()` function can be used to ensure that the 'rooms' array does not exceed 1,00

